reviewText:
Pros:
- good design, materials and quality of assembling;
- all you need in one piece - convenient both sensor and buttons controlling, built-in glowlight, extensible memory;
- a possibility to use enthusiast's firmware patches to jailbreak the device and greatly extend it's functionality from out-of-the-box (I use the reader in Russia and BN's services are useless for me, sorry);
- software stability;
- reasonable price.

Cons: haven't found so far.

There's 2 downsides:
- Very long delivery time (not as long as what amazon said, though);
- Sometimes, when my friend and I plug our smartphones (Galaxy SII && Nexus 5), one of them just won't charge. Don't know if it comes from the car or the adapter.

I like the notebook in the cover but really don't like the corner retaining elastic.  The slide clips designed for the kindle are a far superior option.  I buy moleskine notebook products because of the quality.  The functionality for the kindle cover is just not there e.g.:

- the corner retaining elastic;
- the vertical page holder for the horizontal opening notebook that's sits across the edge of your kindle.  Serves no purpose.

perfect stuff.
works with kindle 3 perfectly;

yes,the notebook is on the left - side, -- just because you cannot put kindle on left ,right?! -- thus bad for the screen
